22149,XYL-RULO,master,Lodge Pole Pine Easel: 70" Height,Lodge Pole Pine Easel: 70" Height,25,415,0,,"<b>The hand peeled look of Lodge pole Pine is unquestionably part of the West's heritage</b><br> <EOL><br> <EOL>* Decorative outdoor log work was a logical extension of the frontier home, where logs were used as a basic building component for just about anything that called for sturdy construction<br> <EOL>* The logs tend to run straight and light colored as a rule. Some suppliers bring in ""beetle kill pine"" with telltale bluish streaks<br> <EOL>* The look speaks of hard working, honest folk who don't have much time for ""frilly stuff""<br> <EOL>* Rustle up a few for yerself and the kinfolk<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Features:</b><br> <EOL>* Rear leg collapses for shipping and storage<br> <EOL>* Adjustable peg system accommodates different sized images for a balanced display<br> <EOL>* Heavyweight logs will support any work, both visually and aesthetically<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Specifications:</b><br> <EOL><b>Height:</b><br> <EOL>* Height of easel: 70""<br> <EOL>* Height of pegs from the floor: 20"", 25"", 30""<br> <EOL>* Peg to peg width: ~ 22""<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Footprint:</b><br> <EOL>* Width: ~ 24""<br> <EOL>* Depth: ~ 22""<br> <EOL>* Diagonal Depth: ~ 24""<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Maximum Image Size:</b><br> <EOL>* Height: 40""<br> <EOL>* Width: 48""<br> <EOL>* Depth: 3""<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Colors:</b> Natural Aspen with beeswax finish<br> <EOL><br> <EOL>* Shipping carton dimensions: 72"" 25"" 5"" <EOL>",,0,1,N,0.010,N,,1,0,0,0,10,Y,58225,Uncategorized/Other crafts,,490.980,,Saturday 17 May 2008 08:39:30 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,157,,398.400,0,N,13,Xylem Design
22260,XYL-886025,master,Lyptus Santa Fe II Easel,Lyptus Santa Fe II Easel,28,1386.500,0,,"* This easel is excellent for most large work<br> <EOL>* An artist can work sitting or standing, with a variety of easily adjusted settings and angles<br> <EOL>* It features a double laminated quad base, side frames and sturdy H-frame construction<br> <EOL>* An adjustable extension on the main frame allows added solidity for larger canvases<br> <EOL><br> <EOL>* The Lyptus Santa Fe II comes with two canvas holders and a painting tray<br> <EOL>* The self-leveling bottom tray/palette features a melamine paint mixing surface with two large stainless steel canisters<br> <EOL>* Its marine style winch raises and lowers easily allowing works weighing up to 200 lbs. Also, the plastic front locking casters offer an ease of mobility<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Features:</b><br> <EOL>* Two canvas holders<br> <EOL>* Painting tray<br> <EOL>* Self-leveling bottom tray/palette<br> <EOL>* Plastic front locking casters<br> <EOL><br> <EOL><b>Specifications:</b><br> <EOL>* Base width/depth: 24""/30""<br> <EOL>* Maximum canvas height: 106""<br> <EOL>* Maximum easel height: 78""<br> <EOL>* Minimum easel height: 129""<br> <EOL>* Bottom painting tray width: 30""",,0,0,N,0.010,N,,1,0,0,0,10,Y,58225,Uncategorized/Other crafts,,1366.380,,Wednesday 21 May 2008 02:47:51 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,157,,1109.200,0,N,13,Xylem Design
